{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The area of a triangle is <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math> square units. If the height of this triangle is <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> units, what is the length, in units, of the base of this triangle?</p>", "keys": ["36"], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math>. The area, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> represents the length of the base of the triangle and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> represents its height. It&rsquo;s given that the triangle has an area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> square units and a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> units. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36 equals one half b left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis\"><mn>36</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36 equals b\"><mn>36</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math>. Thus, the length, in units, of the base of this triangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn></math>.</p>", "externalid": "13e26f81-104e-4cc5-b4b5-52d4234d4b53", "correct_answer": ["36"]}